  "summary": "Prepare for busy weeknights or weekend gatherings with this flavorful <b>Mexican pork roast</b> that gets even better when made ahead. Tender pork loin marinates deeply in an aromatic mixture of earthy achiote paste, freshly squeezed orange juice, tangy lime, and ground spices. Roasted slowly until juicy and golden brown, the meat retains its rich moisture while absorbing vibrant citrus and garlic notes. Slice the roast in advance and store it in its savory baking juices; overnight resting allows the citrus and spice marinade to penetrate the pork completely. Reheating the sliced roast yields an amazingly tender dish that tastes like it was cooked for hours. Serve this fragrant pork with warm corn tortillas, pickled red onions, and fresh cilantro for an easy taco bar or platter feast. The sweet and savory balance of roasted pork infused with authentic Yucatan spices makes this dish a reliable standout. Enjoy stress-free hosting with a spectacular main dish ready whenever you are.",
